leveldb
------------------------------------------
LevelDB is a fast key-value storage library written at Google that provides an
ordered mapping from string keys to string values.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libleveldb-devel-1.23-1bl4
  libleveldb1-1.23-1bl4
  libsnappy1-1.3.1-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  libtcmalloc4-2.19.3-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libbenchmark-devel-1.10.0-1bl1
  libgmock-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  libgtest-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  libsnappy-devel-1.3.1-1
  libtcmalloc-devel-2.19.3-1bl1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/google/leveldb

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/google/leveldb/archive/refs/tags/1.23.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack leveldb-1.23-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./leveldb-1.23-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/leveldb-1.23-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/leveldb-1.23-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libleveldb1-1.23-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libleveldb-devel-1.23-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

